-- title:
--   Lemma 6.1, p. 23 — cost-to-go inequality for NAPP-AL iterates against any stationary point
-- statement:
--   Work in the standing setting of the paper: problem (P) satisfies Assumptions 1 and 2, the step bound $\delta_k$ is set by (8), and $\{w^k\}=\{(u^k,v^k,p^k)\}$ is generated by NAPP-AL with steps $\sigma\delta_k\le\epsilon^k\le\delta_k$. Write $\mathcal L_\gamma$ for the augmented Lagrangian and $\|\cdot\|$ for the Euclidean norm on $\mathbb R^n\times\mathbb R^d\times\mathbb R^m$.
--
--   Fix any stationary point $\bar w$ of (P), so $0\in\partial\mathcal L_\gamma(\bar w)$. Then there is a constant $c_6>0$ such that for every $k\ge0$,
--   $$\mathcal L_\gamma(w^{k+1})-\mathcal L_\gamma(\bar w)\le c_6\big(\|\bar w-w^{k+1}\|^2+\|w^k-w^{k+1}\|^2\big). \tag{37}$$
--
--   The inequality bounds how far the augmented Lagrangian at the next iterate can exceed its value at a stationary point, in terms of the distance to that point and the length of the last step. It is the bridge from an error bound on the distance to the stationary set to the value proximity error bound (Proposition 6.2).
--
--   **Formalization Note** The Lean statement follows the page’s quantifier order: $\bar w$ is fixed before $c_6$ is chosen. Proposition 6.2’s proof needs a uniform estimate because its comparison stationary point varies with $k$; the proof of Lemma 6.1 (pp. 23–26, (38)–(43)) gives constants independent of $\bar w$. "Generated by NAPP-AL" carries the standing setting of Theorem 4.1 (Assumptions 1–2 and rule (8)), because the proof uses the boundedness of $\{w^k\}$ from Theorem 4.1(ii) and the lower bound on $\epsilon^k$ from (8).
-- source:
--   Zhu, Zhao, Zhang, A First-Order Primal-Dual Method for Nonconvex Constrained Optimization Based on the Augmented Lagrangian, arXiv:2007.12219v1, p. 23, Lemma 6.1, display (37); proof pp. 23–26

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_NAPPAL_Subreg_Setting

namespace NAPPAL.Subreg

open NAPPAL.Rate (qseq)
open NAPPAL.KL (wseq)

theorem lemma_6_1 {n d m : ℕ} (P : NAPPAL.KL.Problem n d m) (LG LH L0 : ℝ) (LOmj : Fin m → ℝ)
    (LK : ℝ) (K : NAPPAL.KL.E n → ℝ) (β γ σ : ℝ) (δ ε : ℕ → ℝ)
    (u : ℕ → NAPPAL.KL.E n) (v : ℕ → NAPPAL.KL.E d) (p : ℕ → NAPPAL.KL.E m)
    (hrun : RunHyp P LG LH L0 LOmj LK K β γ σ δ ε u v p)
    (wbar : NAPPAL.KL.W n d m) (hstat : NAPPAL.KL.IsStationary P γ wbar) :
    ∃ c6 : ℝ, 0 < c6 ∧ ∀ k : ℕ,
      NAPPAL.KL.augLag P γ (wseq u v p (k+1)) - NAPPAL.KL.augLag P γ wbar ≤
        c6 * (NAPPAL.KL.wdist wbar (wseq u v p (k+1)) ^ 2 +
          NAPPAL.KL.wdist (wseq u v p k) (wseq u v p (k+1)) ^ 2) := by sorry

end NAPPAL.Subreg
